@vsm 1.2.1
@status(V) production
// LEARNING-RECORD §6 — a document tree policy must be applied by reading the
// FULL node of the decision tree, not one branch; a spec belongs to its plan
// when the PLAN declares it, even if a naive reading of the "no plan → sandbox"
// branch sends it elsewhere. Class-level problem found while applying
// classification_policy_plan.vsm PART III to the corpus (rmw3 directive:
// "lee las especificaciones, si no para qué existen" — read the specs, else
// why do they exist).

learning_record("20260817_tree_application_requires_full_node_read") {
  uuid:      "5f7a9c1e-3b2d-4e6f-9a8c-0d1e2f3a4b5c",
  parent:    "20260817_classification_policy_parametric.vsm (same policy family)",
  family:    "policy-instrumentation",
  class:     "interpretation-gap",
  severity:  "high",
  detection: "rmw3 S5 review 2026-08-17: 'no veo aplicación de la clasificación
             recursiva donde cada directorio es una categoría... spec/ sigue
             estando fuera de plan/'. The previous session read PART II NODO 3
             branch 'NO tiene plan padre → sandbox/' and relocated the 4
             experiment specs (axis2_*, EXP-*) spec/ → sandbox/, leaving spec/
             as a residual readme-only category. But PART III + PART V S3 +
             plan/readme.vsm PLAN-TREE-S4 DECLARE: 'a spec is normally part of
             a plan — there should be NO spec without a plan', specs live in
             plan/<plan>/<fase>/ subfolders, and revision_plan.vsm PH-11-SPEC
             (SPEC-01..04) ALREADY declared those 4 experiments as phases of
             plan VSF-VSL-REVISION-v1. The tree was applied branch-by-branch,
             not node-by-node: the 'NO' branch was executed while the 'SÍ'
             condition (the plan already declares them) was true.",
  root_cause: "the tree (PART II ASCII + PART IV-B rules) was treated as a
             TYPE-based classifier only: read the doc's type, match a rule,
             return a home. But NODO 3 is RELATIONAL: '¿tiene PLAN padre
             activo?' cannot be answered from the spec's own header — it
             requires consulting the PLAN side of the relation (does any
             plan/ root.vsm or the trunk declare this spec as a phase?).
             The instrument lacked that query, so it answered 'no plan' for
             every AXIS2/EXP and sent them all to sandbox/ — including the
             ones the plan already owned. spec/ survived as a category because
             the tree never had a rule that said 'spec WITH a plan lives
             inside the plan'.",
  evidence:  "revision_plan.vsm PH-11-SPEC: {id SPEC-01..04, target:
             spec/axis2_first_loop.spec.vsm ...} (declared 2026-08-06 — the
             plan OWNED the specs before the relocation); classify.py before
             the fix → 'sandbox' for all 4 (type match only); after the fix
             (has_plan_parent query on plan/ tree) → 'plan' for all 4; a
             fixture AXIS2 type NOT declared in any plan → 'sandbox'
             (fall-through works); classification-valid → PASS 108 docs.",
  lesson:    "1) A decision tree node with a RELATIONAL condition (does X own
             Y?) must resolve the relation by consulting the owning side —
             never by assuming the negative from the owned doc's own header.
             2) 'Lee las especificaciones, si no para qué existen': before
             applying a policy, read ALL its parts (PART I..VI), not the one
             branch that matches the current operation; the ASCII tree in
             PART II is the human rendering of PART IV-B rules, and both are
             subordinate to PART III's structural statement (no spec without
             a plan). 3) A residual category (spec/ readme-only) is a smell
             that the tree is incomplete — the category should be REMOVED,
             not kept 'para no romper refs históricas' (refs are remappable:
             relocate_vsm.py remapped 0 broken). 4) The instrument must be
             extended to make the relational query parametric (has_plan_parent
             reads plan/ root.vsm + trunk), so a spec that attaches to a plan
             re-classifies automatically without editing the check.",
  action:    "plan/vsf-vsl-revision/ created as CARPETA (root.vsm ex
             revision_plan + phase-spec/ with the 4 experiments); spec/ root
             category DELETED (git rm readme.vsm); tree_rules: NODO 3 split
             into NORMA-ESPEC-INVESTIGACION (plan_parent=true → plan) +
             NORMA-ESPEC-INVESTIGACION-SIN-PLAN (→ sandbox fall-through);
             classify.py Rule.plan_parent + has_plan_parent() (consults
             plan/plans_active.vsm + plan/*/root.vsm); dir_schema.spec.vsm:
             plan/ category declares AXIS2/EXP + phase-spec files, spec/
             category removed, sandbox/ updated; index.md + core_boot_primer
             (D7 English) + system_map_paper + archive/index + sandbox/readme
             + system_ontology_master refs remapped; boot_manifest hash
             re-based; checks fixtures spec/ → design-sources/.",
  propagation: "Every policy tree with a relational leaf (X owns Y / Y is part
             of X) needs an explicit query for the owning side before applying
             the 'no' branch. When restructuring directories, remove residual
             categories entirely — relocate remaps references, nothing is
             'needed to keep refs alive'. When a plan grows to phases with
             specs, convert it to a folder plan/<plan>/ (root.vsm +
             phase-*/) — the physical structure follows the tree, not the
             reverse (plan/readme.vsm PLAN-TREE-S4).",
  organ:     "S5 (policy, rmw3) → S3 (plan+apply) → S3* (audit the gap) → R4.1 (checks) → pre-commit (gates)",
  recursion: "root system, document layer (spec_revision/plan/)",
  canonical: "docs/spec_revision/plan/classification-policy-plan-v1/classification_policy_plan.vsm (PART II NODO 3, PART III, PART V S3-S4)",
  trace: {
    commit:   "d583a53b (feat(spec_revision): apply plan-as-tree literally — specs live inside plan/<plan>/<fase>/)",
    gate_hit: "R4.1 (classification-valid, dir-schema-valid, agent-map-valid); BOOT-LOAD (boot_manifest hash);
               D7 (core_boot_primer English); full pre-commit EXIT=0",
  },
}
